This Samurai was randomly selected. He's the first one I've taken
beyond the quest. It was my 5th ascension.
Highlights were polying my pet dog into a glass golem on the first few
levels, getting a fountain wish for a GDSM while diluting potions, a
lack of reflection through the quest and the castle. I fought Ashikaga
Takauji with only an "oLS, wand of slow monster, and some wands of fire
to protect me. I got lucky and never died in there, and my pet olog-hai
finished him off for me. I didn't keep the Tsurugi beyond taking it to
my quest leader.
I entered the castle with a wand of cold and a wand of striking. I
didn't meet any soldiers with wands of death, so I was able to wish up
a shield of reflection (I already had some charging scrolls). Later
wishes went to a spellbook of identify and a Helm of brilliance. I had
a robe from when my glass golem killed the minetown priest, and once I
had reflection, I replaced my cloak of displacement with it. Without
the shield, my spell failure rates were decent.
I got Grayswandir from my god while offering for luck; I promptly used
a magic marker to enchant it to +7. Magic markers helped boost my AC;
by the end it was -44.
I tamed a purple worm in Gehennom, and he was a very good pet.
I found Vlad's tower with a lucky ?oMM. He was easy. I got my third
"oLS here.
I cleared the wizard's tower with my pets, then went down and found the
vibrating square. I came back up and killed the wizard. 250hp, AC-44,
140mp. The sanctum was easy, but my purple worm got turned into a baby
crocodile. I used a cursed potion of gain level to leave, then just ran
upstairs. The wizard gave me quite a bit of trouble in some fights; I
needed a potion of full healing once and a "oLS in another. I finally
made it to the planes; there I killed the wizard and his twin with a
wand of death. Unfortunately, I also killed my pet dragon...
Earth, Air, and Fire were all easy. Water was even more relaxing, and I
decided to do a few things in preparation for the astral plane. I wrote
some scrolls of enchant weapon, wielded my unicorn horn to make it more
effective, failed to see the message warning me that I could not wield
a two handed weapon with a shield, and then VAPORIZED GRAYSWANDIR, my
only decent weapon! I still had a 1:3 wand of wishing, so I thought a
bit and wished for the blessed, fixed +2 frost brand. I got it,
fortunately, and I enchanted it to +6. I used a wish on a blessed
figurine of an Archon, who was tame and wielding the Sunsword, and one
more for a second wand of death. Then I stepped through the portal with
him.
I headed to the left with my archon and my angel. I decided to fight
Death first. I kicked down the door, put on my ring of conflict, and
hit Death a couple of times. He died, and I fought through to the
Lawful altar to sacrifice the amulet.



